Windows Internals (Most Important for soc)

services.exe => a vital, legitimate Windows system process that manages background services.
svchost.exe => (Service Host) an essential, legitimate Windows system process that hosts multiple background services.
certutil.exe => a built-in Windows command-line tool used to manage digital certificates, check file hash integrity, and decode files.
lsass.exe => (Local Security Authority Subsystem Service) is a vital Windows system process responsible for enforcing security policies,
managing user logins, and handling password changes.
winlogon.exe => This process is responsible for handling user logon and logoff.
smss.exe => (Session Manager Subsystem) the legitimate Session Manager Subsystem file in Microsoft Windows.
csrss.exe => (Client Server Runtime Subsystem) is a vital, legitimate Windows system process responsible for core functions like managing console windows,
starting and stopping threads,
and handling system shutdowns
wininit.exe => (Windows Initialization Application) a legitimate, critical Windows system process known as the Windows Start-Up Application
explorer.exe => the core Windows process that powers the graphical user interface, including the taskbar, Start menu, desktop, and File Explorer


